<h1>Grammar</h1>
<p>A noun names a person, place or thing. In the sentence <em>The dog barked</em>, the word <em>dog</em> is a noun.</p>
<list type="ol" enum="a"><li>Subject: <em>The dog</em></li><li>Predicate: <em>barked loudly</em></li></list>
<p><sent>The <w>quick</w> fox jumps.</sent></p>
<p>Parts of speech include <strong>nouns</strong>, <strong>verbs</strong> and <strong>adjectives</strong>.</p>
<table><thead><tr><th>Word</th><th>Part of speech</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>run</td><td>verb</td></tr><tr><td>green</td><td>adjective</td></tr></tbody></table>
</level1></bodymatter></book></dtbook>
